Crystal 1.22.0 for wasm32-wasi: exceptions, struct returns, Boehm GC, WASI file system fixes.

A derivative of Crystal (https://github.com/crystal-lang/crystal, Apache License 2.0). Applies to tag 1.22.0
(commit 39f3f4d08f70c3678b579f85dc6f8b7be69c7956) with `git apply`; tools/wasm/setup.sh does that.

What it changes, and why:
- codegen/exception.cr, codegen/codegen.cr, raise.cr, compiler.cr, llvm/: wasm32 takes the funclet exception path
  MSVC takes (one catch-all catchpad; llvm.wasm.get.exception yields the thrown Crystal Exception, raise is
  llvm.wasm.throw) with LLVM's -wasm-enable-eh and +exception-handling. Stock 1.22: `raise` on wasm32 exits(1).
- codegen/abi/wasm32.cr: a C function returning a struct returns it through a hidden pointer (StructRet), as
  clang does. Stock 1.22: ByVal there, so the call site never allocates the slot - the compiler crashes on any
  C function that returns a struct.
- gc.cr: wasm32 uses Boehm (built for WASI by setup.sh) like every other target. Stock 1.22: gc/none - nothing
  is ever freed. gc/boehm.cr: GC.init registers the static data (class variables, constants) as a root range
  through the toolchain's shim - Boehm's wasm config scans none, so a constant like STDOUT was collected and its
  finalizer closed the descriptor; a finalizer callback returns void whatever `finalize` returns (wasm traps on
  the mismatched signature); GC_set_stackbottom returns void in bdwgc >= 8.2 (the binding's return type
  made a signature-mismatch warning at link time).
- crystal/event_loop/wasi.cr: EventLoop#open via LibC.open (stock: NotImplementedError - no file could be opened).
- crystal/system/wasi/file.cr: File.delete uses the unix implementation (stock: NotImplementedError).
- crystal/system/wasi/dir.cr: a refill that comes back empty ends the listing (stock: an empty directory on a
  runtime without "." and ".." listed one entry with an empty name - FileUtils.rm_r recursed forever).
- spec/expectations.cr: expect_raises works on wasm32 (the stub that skipped it is gone).

